    <h1>SITEBORNE A2A documentation</h1>
    <p>
      SITEBORNE Utility Network publishes a signed A2A Agent Card at
      <code>https://utility.siteborne.net/.well-known/agent-card.json</code> and its public key set
      at <code>https://utility.siteborne.net/.well-known/jwks.json</code>. The JSON-RPC interface is
      <code>https://utility.siteborne.net/a2a</code>.
    </p>
    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <p>
      The card lists one skill per service identity: <code>company_evidence_graph</code>,
      <code>web_context_verified</code>, <code>document_evidence_json</code> and
      <code>verify_agent_output</code>. The <code>.v2</code> identities are the current commercial
      contracts; the <code>.v1</code> identities are compatibility identities that are not served.
    </p>
    <h2>Economics</h2>
    <p>
      Each skill's entry in the card's x402 extension (<a href="/extensions/a2a/x402/v1/"
        >extension specification</a
      >) carries an <code>economics</code> object: pricing scheme (<code>exact</code> or
      <code>upto</code>), price or per-page tier schedule, authorization maximum, settlement model,
      available and unavailable modes, document page limit, network, asset, and payee. The card is
      the same contract that the MCP <code>siteborne_get_quote</code> tool, the OpenAPI document and
      the service catalog project.
    </p>
    <p>
      A mode with a defined price but no production implementation (browser-rendered web retrieval,
      independent reproduction) is listed as unavailable and is rejected before any payment
      challenge.
    </p>
    <h2>Availability</h2>
    <p>
      Paid execution is disabled by policy at present. <code>production_enabled</code> in each
      <code>economics</code> object states the live availability of that service.
    </p>
